 "stop": "20 lines",
 "poem": "And I will yet more nectar prepare,\nTo mingle with the waters;\nBut at this time, to my sorrow,\nI shall not be allowed any;\nYet still my darling brood shall follow,\nWhile in her harem's palace\nI leave her naked body,\nAnd their captive bird to devour.\nXIII - THE SPOUSE OF QUEEN MARIA.  The\nQueen: \"My God! how will you answer\nThe urgent desires of Heaven!\nAnd for these woes and troubles,\nWhat is the way to escape?\n\"Here once again I thought upon it,\nSince even now you know nothing.\n\"I had better flee before you,\nAnd promise not aught before;\nIf you then allow any\nThat are useful or hateful alike,\nOr one thing that may please yourself,",
